# ─── Server-only (runtime) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_: these stay on the server.

# Shared with Laravel (same value as its SUGU_EDGE_SECRET), at least 32
# characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. The server signs the visitor's
# address with it on every call made for a visitor (SSR, /api/backend, proxy),
# so Laravel's per-address limits count each visitor rather than this server.
# Unset: no address is sent and Laravel sees this server for everyone.
SUGU_EDGE_SECRET=

# Proxies whose x-forwarded-for entries are skipped when reading the visitor's
# address, as in Laravel. Defaults to Cloudflare's ranges; TRUSTED_PROXIES_EXTRA
# adds the platform's own proxies (addresses or CIDR ranges, comma separated,
# never "*"). This app must only be reachable through the platform proxy.
TRUSTED_PROXIES=
TRUSTED_PROXIES_EXTRA=
